notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Anthropic's report is the account the whole page rests on, and the page reads it as a single-source assessment. Cybersecurity Dive reported Anthropic's warning. The AI Incident Database records the case as Incident 1263, and Paul, Weiss published a client memo on the disclosure. The MITRE page defines Active Scanning, the technique behind stage 02.

The background slides name their own sources: the csoh.org glossary, MITRE ATT&CK and OWASP's GenAI Security Project.

